75 #edb/ref 17592186243071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243629 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243629 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243629 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186242254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243629 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "62df7e56-3c54-5d7e-9fb7-92c76ce4e2dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243639 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186242041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243639 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186242232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243639 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186242649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243639 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186242738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243639 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186243349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243639 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243639 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243639 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186242738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243639 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6652b296-a21e-518a-9c5b-d45f374f2267" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186243639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108323" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:x-3y+2z=12.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7d4770f9-017d-5451-ade2-ef9bc61cba33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244121 #edb/ref 1074 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y+2z & =12 \\\\ 1(7+2t)-3(3+t)+2(1-t) & =12 \\\\ 7+2t-9-3t+2-2t & =12 \\\\ -3t & =12 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2(-4)=-1 \\\\ y=3+(-4)=-1 \\\\ z=1-(-4)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-1,-1,5).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244184 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186243629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244184 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108891" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244184 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244184 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y}{4}=\\frac{1-z}{2},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩=-9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244184 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7ed76edb-2aee-5101-83be-e4a973b64993" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244184 #edb/ref 1074 "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(-2,0,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,4,-2⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-2,0,1⟩+t⟨3,4,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ 4(-2+3t)-3(4t)+(1-2t) & =-9 \\\\ -8+12t-12t+1-2t & =-9 \\\\ -2t & =-2 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(1),4(1),1-2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,4,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(1,4,-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312490 #edb/ref 1080 "(-5,-2,-1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312490 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312490 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3ff6a580-92b7-5851-bcce-fe10c30be1cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313166 #edb/ref 1080 "No intersection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218631316