10,6⟩+s⟨1,0,4⟩+t⟨2,6,0⟩.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314820 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5873c215-84fe-562e-9b4f-b99d76cb6e63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314820 #edb/ref 1074 "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨1,0,4⟩\\times ⟨2,6,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-24i+8j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-24,8,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =⟨-12,10,6⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1,3,2⟩+w⟨-5,-2,-1⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ ⟨1-5w,3-2w,2-w⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ -24(1-5w)+8(3-2w)+6(2-w) & =404 \\\\ -24+120w+24-16w+12-6w & =404 \\\\ 98w & =392 \\\\ w & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=4$ into the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨1-5(4),3-2(4),2-(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-19,-5,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(-19,-5,-2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399622 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399622 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108326" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399622 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399622 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=6+2t \\\\ y=5+t \\\\ z=-3-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x+3y-4z=-43.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417